        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"stael-corinne-5793a277d7a16c1b\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.98,\"analysis\":\"Corinne presents her continued love as an inferred fact about her emotional state: her absence of hatred despite Oswald's betrayal shows that she must still love him. The utterance neither undertakes a relational commitment nor functions as a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":null},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"written\",\"description\":\"The utterance occurs in Corinne's written reply to Oswald: an embedded, inferential avowal equivalent to “I must still love you.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Corinne diagnoses her lingering love from her inability to hate Oswald, even though he has caused her profound suffering. The wider reply confirms the continuing intensity of her attachment while also insisting that duty, religion, and his marriage to her sister require her to renounce seeing him. That renunciation makes the sentence an acknowledgment of feeling rather than a promise to resume their relationship.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"«Il faut que je vous aime encore, pour n'avoir aucun mouvement de haine» (“I must still love you, to feel no stirring of hatred”).\",\"supports\":\"Strong truth-conditional force: Corinne explicitly infers and avows the continued existence of her love from her lack of hatred.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"«la religion seule ne suffirait pas pour me désarmer ainsi»\",\"supports\":\"Her emotional response, rather than religious duty alone, is offered as further evidence that the love remains.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The passage is headed «RÉPONSE DE CORINNE» and later says that she has renounced seeing Oswald because he is another woman's husband.\",\"supports\":\"Establishes the written-reply setting and weighs against performative commitment: she acknowledges love while refusing renewed union or contact.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The sentence is part of a sustained retrospective explanation of resentment, suffering, impaired reason, admiration, and love.\",\"supports\":\"Its reflective and evidential structure supports an avowal or report rather than an independently reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is identified in Madame de Staël's Corinne; ou, l'Italie, CHAPITRE III, with affirmative present form and the modifier «encore».\",\"supports\":\"Confirms the textual location and the explicit present persistence of the loving state.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core force as a reflective, inferential avowal of continuing love. The emotional intensity and renunciatory context require contextual explanation but create no residual pressure beyond T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The modal phrase «il faut que» is epistemic or inferential here (“I must still love you”), not an expression of obligation to love.\"}"
        }
      ],
